{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumCompletedSquare","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumCompletedSquare","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumBetaCoordinates","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Chebyshev"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.eight_mul_card_mul_sum_hookZ_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.eight_mul_card_mul_sum_hookZ_ge","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumCompletedSquare.lean#L96-L122","doc":"**Cauchy–Schwarz floor on the hook sum.**\n\n`(Σ_i d_i)² − L·Σ_i a_i² ≤ 8L·Σ_c h(c)`.  Since `Σ_i d_i = 2 Σ_i β_i − Σ_i a_i` is fixed by\n`(n, L)` alone (identity (III), `two_mul_sum_betaR`), the left-hand side is a constant of\n`(n, L)` — so this is a parameter-free lower bound on the hook sum, hence on the energy.\n\nMeasured tight: against `H_min(n)` at `L = k` the gap is exactly `0` at every triangular `n`\ntested (`rev_energy_gap_rigidity_probe.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.eight_mul_sum_hookZ_completedSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.eight_mul_sum_hookZ_completedSquare","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumCompletedSquare.lean#L70-L94","doc":"**The hook sum is a positive-definite quadratic in the β-numbers.**\n\n`8 Σ_c h(c) = Σ_{i<L} (2β_i − a_i)² − Σ_{i<L} a_i²` for any padding `L ≥ ℓ(μ)`.  The second sum\ndepends only on `L`, so all of the diagram-dependence is the sum of squares. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookDev_sub_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookDev_sub_succ","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumCompletedSquare.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**The rigidity, exactly.** `d_i − d_{i+1} = 2(β_i − β_{i+1}) − 4`: the deviations are\nconstant iff every β-gap is `2`, and each unit of gap-deviation moves `d` by `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookDev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookDev","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumCompletedSquare.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The row-`i` deviation `d_i = 2β_i − a_i`.  Constant exactly on the staircase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookCentre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hookCentre","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumCompletedSquare.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The centre of the hook sum's quadratic in row `i` at `L` rows: `a_i = 2L − 3 − 4i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}